COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[520,"§Qaf, Adh-Dhariyat\ndeeds\nMaintain with care the five daily prayers in congregation at the mosque.\nAfter performing Al-Fajr prayer, stay and glorify Allah until sunrise.\nGo to the mosque before Al-Maghrib prayer, sit and glorify Allah until sunset.\nguid\nA wise person is the one who learns a lesson from what happened to others.\nEnsure the clarity of the heart from overwhelming sicknesses, so that it benefits from admonishments.\nPatience and glorification of Allah are coupled together, so ensure to maintain them.\nrefl\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَذِكۡرَىٰ لِمَن كَانَ لَهُۥ قَلۡبٌ أَوۡ أَلۡقَى ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيدٞ ٣٧\nThe one who listens attentively to the revelations of Allah, and listens to them by way of seeking guidance from them, with presence of mind. For such a person there is also a reminder, exhortation, healing and guidance. But as for the one who turns away and does not lend an ear to the revelations, they will not benefit him at all, because he is not receptive and the wisdom of Allah does not dictate that such a person should be guided. Al-Saadi: 807.\nWhat benefit can be gained from the Quran for one who does not listen to it with mindful heart and attentive ear?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَذِكۡرَىٰ لِمَن كَانَ لَهُۥ قَلۡبٌ أَوۡ أَلۡقَى ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيدٞ ٣٧\nHere, (or) is used instead of \"and\" because those who benefit from the verses are two types: First: One who has a mindful heart, which is sufficed by the least hint. He does not need to work hard to make his heart attentive, rather, his heart is alert, pure, and ready for guidance, not turning away from it, and therefore, his heart needs only to receive the guidance. Second: A person who lacks readiness and willingness, but, when guidance comes to him, he listens attentively, brings his heart into mindfulness, and gathers his thoughts, and so, he realizes its goodness and truth by his contemplation and inference. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/16.\nIn this verse, (or) is used instead of \"and\". Why?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ قَبۡلَ طُلُوعِ ٱلشَّمۡسِ وَقَبۡلَ ٱلۡغُرُوبِ ٣٩\nTo help His Messenger (ﷺ) to bear patiently what they say, Allah directed him to glorify His praise before sunrise and before sunset, during the night and after the prayers. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/26.\nWhat are the things that help one become patient?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ قَبۡلَ طُلُوعِ ٱلشَّمۡسِ وَقَبۡلَ ٱلۡغُرُوبِ ٣٩ وَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَسَبِّحۡهُ وَأَدۡبَٰرَ ٱلسُّجُودِ ٤٠\n(So bear patiently what they say) of criticism and rejection of the message you have brought. Distract yourself from them by focusing on your Lord and glorifying Him, at the beginning and end of the day, and during the night and after the prayers, for remembering Allah consoles and brings comfort to the heart, and helps one to be patient. Al-Saadi: 807.\nWhat is the wisdom behind enjoining the glorification of Allah after enjoining patience?\nوَسَبِّحۡ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّكَ قَبۡلَ طُلُوعِ ٱلشَّمۡسِ وَقَبۡلَ ٱلۡغُرُوبِ ٣٩\nAl-Razi said: \"Know that the reward for the one’s words commensurate with the extent of their emanation from his knowledge and wisdom, the eye of his heart turns as his tongue does [with his words], and he perceives their facts and meanings. Glorifying Allah is exalting Him above everything that may be conceited by illusion, pictured in the imagination, plotted by the senses, or conjured up by the premonitions. Praising Allah reveals His great favors [upon His servants], and Him being the exclusive source of all the blessings.\" Al-Biqai: 18/439.\nWhat is meant by the glorification of Allah?\nوَمَآ أَنتَ عَلَيۡهِم بِجَبَّارٖۖ\n(And you are not there to compel them), it is not you who forces them to accept guidance; this is not part of your mission, so you cannot make them believe it, for you are only conveying the Message. Ibn Kathir: 7/412.\nWhat is precisely the duty of the preacher to Allah?\nوَٱلذَّٰرِيَٰتِ ذَرۡوٗا ١ فَٱلۡحَٰمِلَٰتِ وِقۡرٗا ٢ فَٱلۡجَٰرِيَٰتِ يُسۡرٗا ٣ فَٱلۡمُقَسِّمَٰتِ أَمۡرًا ٤ إِنَّمَا تُوعَدُونَ لَصَادِقٞ ٥ وَإِنَّ ٱلدِّينَ لَوَٰقِعٞ ٦\nAllah swore by these things because of their unique abilities and functions that are extraordinary, hence, whoever is capable of creating them, is indeed capable of the promised resurrection. Al-Shawkani: 5/83.\nAllah swore by these creations. Why?\nwords\nبَطشًاStriking power\nفَنَقَّبُواThey moved about\nمَحِيصٍAn escape\nلُغُوبٍWeariness\nسِرَاعًاThey emerge rapidly\nوَالذَّارِيَاتِBy the winds that scatter dust\nفَالحَامِلاَتِ وِقرًاAnd by the clouds carrying loads of water\nفَالجَارِيَاتِ يُسرًاAnd by the ships that sail with ease"],[521,"§Adh-Dhariyat\ndeeds\nSet your alarm clock to a time before dawn, rise and ask Allah for forgiveness.\nAllocate a fixed amount from your income -even if little- for the beggar and the deprived.\nInvite a friend of yours to your house for a meal and be generous with him.\nguid\nRemembering the ways of the righteous helps to act like them.\nBe certain that Allah has guaranteed your provision.\nThe story of Abraham (u) is a great one that is full of lessons and admonishments.\nrefl\nإِنَّكُمۡ لَفِي قَوۡلٖ مُّخۡتَلِفٖ ٨ يُؤۡفَكُ عَنۡهُ مَنۡ أُفِكَ ٩\nThe conflicting views concerning the Prophet (ﷺ) and the Quran, which are total fabrications because when they denied the truth, their methods, views, ways, and sayings became divided. The truth is one and a straight path, and whoever opposed it, his ways and methods would become numerous, as Allah says, (But they denied the truth when it came to them, so they are in a state of confusion) [50:5], which means bewilderment and uncertainty. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/32-33.\nAdhering to the revelation is one of the reasons for unity. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ فِي جَنَّٰتٖ وَعُيُونٍ ١٥\nTo the scholars of the Islamic jurisprudence fundamentals [Fiqh fundamentals], this verse is clear proof of the fact that the cause for attaining these gardens and springs is righteousness. Al-Shanqiti: 7/439.\nThe cause for entering Paradise is inferred in the news about the righteous. Explain.\nءَاخِذِينَ مَآ ءَاتَىٰهُمۡ رَبُّهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ قَبۡلَ ذَٰلِكَ مُحۡسِنِينَ ١٦\n(Receiving what their Lord will give them), this could mean that the Lord has given the people of Paradise all that they wished for, of all kinds of delights, which they receive with contentment and bring them joy and delight, and they do not ask for any alternative or seek any change. Or it may be that this is a description of the righteous in this world; they accept what Allah gives of commands and prohibitions. In other words, they welcome them open-heartedly. Al-Saadi: 808.\nWhat is the distinguishing trait of the righteous in this worldly life?\nكَانُواْ قَلِيلٗا مِّنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ مَا يَهۡجَعُونَ ١٧\nThe aim of this verse is to show that they endure worship during the times of rest, and do not ease off from the hardships of the day except a little. Alhasan said that they endured nighttime prayers, and did not sleep except for a short time. Abdulla bin Masoud said: They slept for a little while, then woke up praying the rest of the night. Al-Alusi: 27/14.\nWhat did the righteous do, during sleep and resting times, to deserve Paradise and bliss?\nوَبِٱلۡأَسۡحَارِ هُمۡ يَسۡتَغۡفِرُونَ ١٨\nPredawn time is singled out for mention because it is when people are overtaken by sleep. Their prayers and the seeking of forgiveness before dawn are more wondrous than at other parts of the night. Moreover, the verse indicates their repeated prayers at predawn. Ibn Ashur: 26/350.\nPredawn time is singled out for mention. Why?\nوَفِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ رِزۡقُكُمۡ وَمَا تُوعَدُونَ ٢٢ فَوَرَبِّ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ إِنَّهُۥ لَحَقّٞ مِّثۡلَ مَآ أَنَّكُمۡ تَنطِقُونَ ٢٣\nA wise man said: It means that just as each person speaks with his tongue and not with someone else's tongue, each person will consume his provision that is allocated for him and cannot consume someone else's provision. Al-Baghawi: 19/231.\nThe provision is likened to speech. Why?\nفَرَاغَ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِۦ\nAbraham (u) rushed back to his household almost without being noticed. This is considered a part of the host’s generosity where he can go to arrange for food without being noticed by the guest. Unlike a host who makes the guest hear what is happening by saying: Wait until I bring you food, or similar to that, which makes the guest feel uncomfortable. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/45.\nDescribe one of the signs of the Prophet’s (p) generosity and their good manners.\nwords\nذَاتِ الحُبُكِPerfectly created with orbits for planets\nيُؤفَكُ عَنهُ(ﷺ) Diverted from the Quran and the Prophet\nقُتِلَ الخَرَّاصُونَCursed are the liars\nيَهجَعُونَThey sleep\nمُنكَرُونَUnknown people to him\nفَرَاغَHe went quickly\nفَأَوجَسَ مِنهُمHe felt apprehensive about them"],[522,"§Adh-Dhariyat\ndeeds\nWhen the wind blows, ask Allah for its good, and seek refuge with Him from its evil.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask Your forgiveness and repent to You,\" a hundred times.\nWhen you go to bed, say, \"O Allah, I submitted my soul to You, I have turned my face toward You, I entrusted my affair to You, and committed my back to You in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge or haven from You except with You. I believed in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.\"\nguid\nDo not be deluded by your power or wealth, lest you will be deprived of guidance.\nReflect on the reasons for the demise of past nations.\nTurn to Allah, the Almighty, in all situations.\nrefl\n۞قَالَ فَمَا خَطۡبُكُمۡ أَيُّهَا ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ٣١\nAbraham (u) asked them after he provided them with food. He followed the customary way of not asking guests about their objectives until they were ready to leave, so they would not feel unwelcome and to provide help if possible when needed. Ibn Ashur: 27/5.\nAbraham (u) asked the angels after he provided them with food. Why?\nفَمَا وَجَدۡنَا فِيهَا غَيۡرَ بَيۡتٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ٣٦\n(But We only found in it one Muslim household), Qatadah said: If there was more than one household, Allah would have saved them so that they would know that Allah protects the faith, and that the faithful would never be forsaken. Al-Tabari: 22/430.\nFaith has a great value for the household. Explain.\nوَتَرَكۡنَا فِيهَآ ءَايَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ يَخَافُونَ ٱلۡعَذَابَ ٱلۡأَلِيمَ ٣٧\nThis verse indicates that the signs of Allah and the wonders that He created in this world have traces pointing to Him and to the truthfulness of His Messengers, benefit only those who believe in the resurrection and fear Allah's punishment. Those who do not believe in the Hereafter would say: These doomed people were only destroyed by time, like others before them had, for time is the giver of happiness and misery. But, those who believe in the Hereafter and are apprehensive of it benefit from these signs and admonishments. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/49-50.\nWho benefits from the narrations and admonishments of the Quran?\nفَمَا ٱسۡتَطَٰعُواْ مِن قِيَامٖ وَمَا كَانُواْ مُنتَصِرِينَ ٤٥\nThey were unable to arise after the punishment struck them, nor could they rise afterward. Qatadah said: They did not come up after the punishment. (Nor could they defend themselves), Qatadah said: They did not have the power to defend themselves against Allah. Al-Baghawi: 4/233.\nIn light of this verse, how do you understand this Prophetic Hadith: \"Allah gives respite to the oppressor. But when He seizes him, He does not let him escape\"?\nوَمِن كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ خَلَقۡنَا زَوۡجَيۡنِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَذَكَّرُونَ ٤٩\nThe aim of taking heed is remembering all that is mentioned about the Last Day gathering and resurrection because the One Who is capable of creating all that is certainly capable of resurrecting the dead on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Alusi: 27/27.\nThis verse indicates Allah’s capability to resurrect the dead. How?\nفَفِرُّوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ إِنِّي لَكُم مِّنۡهُ نَذِيرٞ مُّبِينٞ ٥٠\nOrdinary people flee from ignorance to knowledge willfully and hastily, from idleness to revitalization cautiously but firmly, and from hardship to prosperity with confidence and hope. Al-Biqai: 18/447.\nHow do people flee to Allah?\nفَفِرُّوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ إِنِّي لَكُم مِّنۡهُ نَذِيرٞ مُّبِينٞ ٥٠\nAllah describes turning to Him as fleeing, because turning to anyone other than Him will result in all kinds of fearful outcomes and troubles, whereas turning to Him leads to all that one loves, security, joy, happiness and triumph. The servant would flee from Allah's Divine Will and Decree to His Divine Will and Decree. Al-Saadi: 812.\nAllah describes turning to Him as fleeing. Why?\nwords\nمُسَوَّمَةًMarked for the transgressors\nفَتَوَلَّى بِرُكنِهِHe turned away with his supporters\nفَنَبَذنَاهُم فِي اليَمِّWe cast them into the sea\nمُلِيمٌBlameworthy\nالعَقِيمَA devastating barren wind\nمَا تَذَرُIt spared nothing\nكَالرَّمِيمِDisintegrated ruins\nفَعَتَواThey insolently defied"],[523,"§Adh-Dhariyat, At-Tur\ndeeds\nAdvise a Muslim and remind him using a kind and pleasant approach.\nAsk Allah to help you in today's work.\nRecall one of your worldly needs and ask Allah to fulfill it for you.\nguid\nAllah created us to worship Him; did we do that?\nKnow that Allah provides provisions to all, and He is Free of need.\nDo not hasten the punishment of the disbelievers, for Allah gives respite but never neglects.\nrefl\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنۡهُمۡ فَمَآ أَنتَ بِمَلُومٖ ٥٤ وَذَكِّرۡ فَإِنَّ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ تَنفَعُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥٥\nHaving commanded His Messenger (ﷺ) to turn away from them, Allah commanded him not to neglect reminding and admonishing in the best manner. Al-Shawkani: 5/92.\nThere is a useful preaching lesson in the command to keep reminding after being commanded to turn away. Explain.\nوَذَكِّرۡ فَإِنَّ ٱلذِّكۡرَىٰ تَنفَعُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٥٥\nAllah limits the justification of His command of reminding to one reason, which is its benefit to the believers since that is realized, and to show concern for them at the same time there is disregard of the disbelievers. Allah says, (So remind, if the reminder should benefit ` The reminder will be received by him who fears Allah ` But it will be avoided by the wretched)[87:9-11]. Ibn Ashur: 27/24.\nAllah limits the justification of His command of reminding to its benefit to the believers. Why?\nوَمَا خَلَقۡتُ ٱلۡجِنَّ وَٱلۡإِنسَ إِلَّا لِيَعۡبُدُونِ ٥٦\nThe mention of jinn precedes mankind in this verse because the polytheists showed interest in what they considered a strange piece of information about the jinn, whom they used to worship, so that they would know that the jinn were only servants of Allah. Ibn Ashur: 27/28.\nThe mention of jinn precedes mankind in this verse. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلرَّزَّاقُ ذُو ٱلۡقُوَّةِ ٱلۡمَتِينُ ٥٨\nBy His might He causes His provision to reach all the worlds. Al-Saadi: 813.\nAllah's attribute, (the Mighty) is mentioned after (the All-Provider). Why?\nوَٱلطُّورِ ١ وَكِتَٰبٖ مَّسۡطُورٖ ٢ فِي رَقّٖ مَّنشُورٖ ٣ وَٱلۡبَيۡتِ ٱلۡمَعۡمُورِ ٤ وَٱلسَّقۡفِ ٱلۡمَرۡفُوعِ ٥ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِ ٱلۡمَسۡجُورِ ٦ إِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ لَوَٰقِعٞ ٧ مَّا لَهُۥ مِن دَافِعٖ ٨\nOmar (t) went out checking the welfare of Muslims and passed by the house of a man who was standing in voluntary prayer. Omar stood quietly, listening to his recitation; the man was reciting, (By the mount of Tur), until he reached (The punishment of your Lord will surely come to pass ` There is none who can avert it) Omar said, \"By the Lord of the Ka'bah, this is a true oath.\" Omar dismounted his donkey and sat next to a wall for a while. He then went back to his house and fell ill for a month. During his illness, people would visit him, not knowing what caused his illness. Ibn Kathir: 4/242.\nCan someone reflect on the meanings of the Quran by listening to it? Explain.\nوَٱلۡبَيۡتِ ٱلۡمَعۡمُورِ ٤\nAnas bin Malik reported on the authority of Malik bin Sa'sa'a, a person of his tribe, that Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Then the frequented House was raised to me. I said: O Gabriel! What is this? He replied: It is the frequented House (Al-Bait Al-Ma'mur); seventy thousand angels enter it daily, and after they come out, they never return.\" Al-Tabari: 22/455.\nThe frequented House (Al-Bait Al-Ma'mur) has a great status. What is the proof for that?\nفَوَيۡلٞ يَوۡمَئِذٖ لِّلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ١١ ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ فِي خَوۡضٖ يَلۡعَبُونَ ١٢\nAllah describes the knowledge they used to have as falsehood, which is ill speech, and describes their deeds as amusement, which is wasted effort. Hence, they neither had useful knowledge, nor righteous deeds. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/55.\nThis verse mentions the most prominent traits of the deniers. What are they?\nwords\nأَتَوَاصَوا بِهِDid they suggest this denial to each other?\nطَاغُونَTransgressing people\nذَنُوبًاA share of punishment\nوَالطُّورِBy the mount of Tur, where Allah spoke to Moses (u)\nفِي رَقٍّ مَنشُورٍIn parchment spread open\nالمَسجُورِOverflowed\nتَمُورُIt will convulse violently\nيُدَعُّونَThey will be violently shoved"],[524,"§At-Tur\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah! We ask You for guidance, righteousness, chastity and self-sufficiency.\"\nFast for a day for the sake of Allah.\nGive a needy person some meat and fruit.\nguid\nStrive to fear Allah, so that you will enjoy His Paradise.\nBe among those who are fearful of Allah in this worldly life, as He describes them.\nHelp your parents to become righteous because you will be joined with them in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nٱصۡلَوۡهَا فَٱصۡبِرُوٓاْ أَوۡ لَا تَصۡبِرُواْ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡۖ إِنَّمَا تُجۡزَوۡنَ مَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٦ إِنَّ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ فِي جَنَّٰتٖ وَنَعِيمٖ ١٦\nHaving mentioned the punishment of the deniers, Allah now mentions the bliss of the righteous to combine encouragement and warning, and so the hearts remain in a state between fear and hope. Al-Saadi: 814.\nAllah mentions the bliss of the righteous after the punishment of the deniers. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ فِي جَنَّٰتٖ وَنَعِيمٖ ١٧ فَٰكِهِينَ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰهُمۡ رَبُّهُمۡ وَوَقَىٰهُمۡ رَبُّهُمۡ عَذَابَ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ١٨\nThis, also, indicates that saving the righteous from the punishment of Hellfire is part of justice since they did not commit what they should be punished for. However, the bliss they receive is a bounty and honor from Allah to them. Ibn Ashur: 27/46.\nIn this verse, Allah combines His justice and bounty. Explain.\nمُتَّكِـِٔينَ عَلَىٰ سُرُرٖ مَّصۡفُوفَةٖۖ\nAllah describes the thrones as being arranged in rows so as to indicate that they will be numerous and well organized, and the people sitting on them are together and happy, treating one another kindly, and speaking gentle words to one another. Al-Saadi: 815.\nDescribing the thrones as being arranged in rows indicates few things. Explain.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱتَّبَعَتۡهُمۡ ذُرِّيَّتُهُم بِإِيمَٰنٍ أَلۡحَقۡنَا بِهِمۡ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمۡ وَمَآ أَلَتۡنَٰهُم مِّنۡ عَمَلِهِم مِّن شَيۡءٖۚ كُلُّ ٱمۡرِيِٕۢ بِمَا كَسَبَ رَهِينٞ ٢١\n(And those who believe and their offspring follow them), the meaning of this verse is explained in this Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: \"Allah will raise the rank of the believer's offspring to be with him in Paradise, even if they are less than him in deeds, to please him.\" This is honoring the offspring because of their parents. In the Arabic text, the word (faith) is in an indefinite form which indicates that their amount of faith was not high enough to make them reach their parent's rank, but Allah joined them together in honor of their parents. If this was attained with their little faith, then what if their faith was great? (And will not detract anything from their deeds), We will not detect the reward of their deeds, rather, We will give them the reward in full. Ibn Juzay: 2/376.\nThe pleasure of the people in Paradise will be complete. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا كُنَّا قَبۡلُ فِيٓ أَهۡلِنَا مُشۡفِقِينَ ٢٦ فَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡنَا وَوَقَىٰنَا عَذَابَ ٱلسَّمُومِ ٢٧\nThis verse indicates that the intense fear of Allah’s punishment in this worldly life is a reason for being saved from His punishment in the Hereafter. Conversely, whoever does not fear Allah’s punishment in this worldly life, will not be saved from His punishment in the Hereafter. Al-Shanqiti: 7/457.\nState the reason for being saved from punishment in the Hereafter, and what is inferred by this verse.\nقَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا كُنَّا قَبۡلُ فِيٓ أَهۡلِنَا مُشۡفِقِينَ ٢٦\nMeaning: We were afraid and apprehensive, so we refrained from sin out of fear of Him, and we corrected our faults. Al-Saadi: 814.\nWhen can the fear of Allah and the Hereafter be useful to a person?\nإِنَّا كُنَّا مِن قَبۡلُ نَدۡعُوهُۖ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡبَرُّ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٢٨\nAll those in the heavens and earth ask Allah; nevertheless, attaining salvation is through sincere worship and devotion to Allah, not by merely asking for it. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/62.\nAll created beings ask Allah, the Almighty, but who will be saved from the Scorching Fire?\nwords\nاصلَوهَاEnter and burn therein\nمَصفُوفَةٍLined up, facing each other\nبِحُورٍFair women of Paradise\nرَهِينٌHe will be accountable for what he earned\nيَتَنَازَعُونَThey will pass around to one another\nلاَ لَغوٌ فِيهَاNo ill speech while drinking it\nوَلاَ تَأثِيمٌNo commission of sin because of it\nمَكنُونٌWell-protected\nعَذَابَ السَّمُومِThe punishment of the Scorching Fire"],[525,"§At-Tur\ndeeds\nReflect on a plot by those who oppose the religion, and ask Allah to rebound it against them.\nDo your utmost to maintain Al-Fajr prayer.\nMaintain the daily remembrance of Allah in the morning and evening.\nguid\nThe Prophets (p) never took reward for calling others to Allah.\nWhen Allah seals up someone's heart, he will never benefit from warning signs.\nWorship and glorification of Allah are important for the tranquility of a Muslim's soul.\nrefl\nأَمۡ تَأۡمُرُهُمۡ أَحۡلَٰمُهُم بِهَٰذَآۚ أَمۡ هُمۡ قَوۡمٞ طَاغُونَ ٣٢\nMeaning: It is not possible that their minds prompted them to say such things because prudent minds do not prompt such things. This alludes to the fact that they actually lost their minds by saying that since sound minds do not prompt such things, and so, they resemble mindless people. This explains what is narrated that the disbeliever lacks a mind. Ibn Ashur: 27/64.\nHow do you explain the saying that the disbeliever lacks a mind?\nأَمۡ تَأۡمُرُهُمۡ أَحۡلَٰمُهُم بِهَٰذَآۚ أَمۡ هُمۡ قَوۡمٞ طَاغُونَ ٣٢\nMeaning: Their minds prompt them to say these contradicting accusations about the Prophet (ﷺ) that he was a soothsayer or a madman. A soothsayer is exceedingly intelligent and insightful, while a madman lacks a basic mind, let alone intelligence or insight. Al-Shawkani: 5/99.\nExplain the polytheists contradicting accusations about the Prophet (ﷺ).\nفَلۡيَأۡتُواْ بِحَدِيثٖ مِّثۡلِهِۦٓ إِن كَانُواْ صَٰدِقِينَ ٣٤\n(If they are truthful), in their claim that he (ﷺ) made it up, hence, if they could not produce a statement like it, then they are liars. This entices them to try to match the Quran so that when they could not do it, it would be evidence of their lies. Ibn Ashur: 27/67.\nWhat is the purpose of the statement (If they are truthful), mentioned in the verse?\nفَلۡيَأۡتُواْ بِحَدِيثٖ مِّثۡلِهِۦٓ إِن كَانُواْ صَٰدِقِينَ ٣٤\nNormally, it is not possible for a person, who belongs to a group of people, and shares similar capabilities with them, to produce something so great that they all are unable to match it. A sane person will not assert something [producing the like of the Quran] without being fully aware of it. Their awareness entails their capability to match the Quran. The Prophet (ﷺ) shares with them eloquent speech, home, and kinship ties. In fact, some of them may exceed him in writing, poetry, mixing with scholars, practicing oratory, producing letters, etc. So, the Prophet (ﷺ) was capable of bringing something inimitable only with divine help, and that was the aim of their denial. Al-Biqai: 19/26.\nThis verse presents a clear proof of the truthfulness of the Prophet’s (ﷺ) Message. Explain\nيَوۡمَ لَا يُغۡنِي عَنۡهُمۡ كَيۡدُهُمۡ شَيۡـٔٗا وَلَا هُمۡ يُنصَرُونَ ٤٦\nMeaning: Not a small or great, even though in this world they may be able to survive for a short time by means of their plots. But on the Day of Resurrection, their plots will come to naught, and their efforts will prove worthless. Al-Saadi: 818.\nWhat is the difference between the disbelievers' plots in this life and in the Hereafter?\nوَإِنَّ لِلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ عَذَابٗا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٧\nIt is said that they will be punished before their death. Ibn Zaid said: The punishments are worldly afflictions such as deceases, disasters, and the loss of wealth and offspring. Al-Qurtubi: 19/541.\nAllah’s punishment of the wrongdoer is not limited to the Hereafter. Explain.\nوَمِنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ فَسَبِّحۡهُ وَإِدۡبَٰرَ ٱلنُّجُومِ ٤٩\nThis is attained by performing Al-Fajr prayer and its sunnah since that is when the stars fade away. Hence, the morning worship is exhorted twice to honor its status because it is a reason for being saved from imminent punishment, and a cause for achieving victory over a well-armed enemy of the apparent and deceitful hypocrites. Al-Biqai: 19/39.\nWhen the stars fade away is a time singled out for praying and glorification of Allah. Why?\nwords\nأَحلاَمُهُمTheir minds\nطَاغُونَTransgressing people\nتَقَوَّلَهُHe has made this [Quran] up\nمِن مَغرَمٍThey are overburdened by debt\nكَيدًاA plot\nكِسفًاPieces\nمَركُومٌClouds heaped up\nيُصعَقُونَThey will be struck down\nوَإِدبَارَ النُّجُومِGlorify Him at night and when the stars fade away"],[526,"§An-Najm\ndeeds\nRead about the events of Al-Isra' and Miraj (Night Journey and the Ascension into Heavens) as related by Allah's Messenger (ﷺ).\nAsk Allah for guidance, chastity and self-sufficiency.\nAfter hearing the Adhan, say : \"O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and established prayer. Grant Muhammad (ﷺ) the intercession and favor, and raise him to the praiseworthy position You have promised him.\" So that our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) will intercede for you.\nguid\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) has a very high rank with Allah.\nBelieving in the angel Gabriel (u), respecting him, and acknowledging that he came down with the revelation from Allah to the Prophet (ﷺ).\nThe disbelievers do not venerate Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلنَّجۡمِ إِذَا هَوَىٰ ١ مَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمۡ وَمَا غَوَىٰ ٢\nAllah swears by the stars to the soundness of what the Messenger (ﷺ) brought of divine revelation, because there is something amazing in common between the two. Allah has made the stars an adornment for the heaven, and similarly, He has made the revelation and its effects an adornment for the earth. If it were not for the knowledge inherited from the Prophets, the people would be in darkness greater than that of the darkest night. Al-Saadi: 818.\nWhat is the link between the stars and the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ)?\nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمۡ وَمَا غَوَىٰ ٢\nThis verse is the result of the oath; it is addressed to the tribe of Quraish, and (your companion) is Muhammad (ﷺ). So, Allah rules out straying and erring on the part of the Prophet (ﷺ). The difference between them is that straying is unintentional while erring is. Ibn Juzay: 2/380.\nWhat is the difference between straying and erring?\nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمۡ وَمَا غَوَىٰ ٢ وَمَا يَنطِقُ عَنِ ٱلۡهَوَىٰٓ ٣ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا وَحۡيٞ يُوحَىٰ ٤\nAllah rules out straying and erring from the Prophet (ﷺ), and describes him as one who does not speak out of his own desire, but a revelation revealed. So, Allah rules out the desires and affirms the complete knowledge, which is the revelation. The negation of desires indicates the perfect intent, and the affirmation of revelation indicates the perfect knowledge and Allah describes the Prophet's opponents with the opposite of these two traits. The human perfection is attained by completing the submission to Allah through knowledge and intent. Ibn Taimyah: 6/128.\nThis verse confirmed the Prophet's (ﷺ) perfection and the polytheists' deficiency. Explain.\nوَمَا يَنطِقُ عَنِ ٱلۡهَوَىٰٓ ٣ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا وَحۡيٞ يُوحَىٰ ٤\nThis indicates that the Sunnah is also revealed from Allah to His Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 818.\nHow does this verse explain the stature of the Sunnah?\nمَا زَاغَ ٱلۡبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغَىٰ ١٧\nAllah negates His Prophet's turning his gaze to every side and extending his sight beyond his limit, like a person who lacks etiquette when he is present before kings and greats. Allah relates that he was in such complete control of himself and so exclusively attentive that he kept his mind and his sight focused on the object for which he had been summoned. He maintained a great composure, and tranquility of heart, which reflected the ultimate human perfection. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/76.\nThis verse indicates the Prophet's (ﷺ) perfect etiquette during Al-Isra’ and Al-Miraj journey. Explain.\nإِن يَتَّبِعُونَ إِلَّا ٱلظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهۡوَى ٱلۡأَنفُسُۖ\nMeaning: Whatever their souls, the persistent enjoiners of evil, lust for. A human soul always longs for less than the best because it is prone to the love of pleasures; it is driven to what yields the best outcome for it only by reason. Al-Alusi: 14/58.\nHow does one make the best out of himself from this verse?\nوَلَقَدۡ جَآءَهُم مِّن رَّبِّهِمُ ٱلۡهُدَىٰٓ ٢٣\nThe wisdom dictates that whoever recognizes guidance, should follow it, even if it comes from his enemy, so, how about if this guidance comes from One Who is superior to him, One Whose benevolence never ceases to reach him? Al-Biqai: 19/61.\nWhat is inferred from this verse: (And there has come to them guidance from their Lord)?\nwords\nوَالنَّجمِ إِذَا هَوَىBy the star when it descends\nوَمَا غَوَىHe has not erred\nذُو مِرَّةٍHe is powerful with good looks\nفَتَدَلَّىHe approached\nأَفَتُمَارُونَهُand deny him ﷺ Do you dispute with Muhammad\nسِدرَةِ المُنتَهَىThe Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary in the Seventh heaven. It is the final destination for everything ascending from earth, and everything descending from above it"],[527,"§An-Najm\ndeeds\nLook for a gathering of Quran recital or an Islamic study circle and join them even for a short while.\nSay, \"O Allah, make me love belief and adorn my heart with it, and Make me hate disbelief, deviance, and rebellion.\"\nLook for a major sin committed in your country and warn those whom you know of it.\nguid\nKeep in mind that Allah is All-Knowing of everyone who strayed and who is guided.\nFrom this Surah, become familiar with the vastness of Allah's forgiveness and mercy.\nEvery person will be recompensed for his deeds, whether good or evil.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ لَيُسَمُّونَ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ تَسۡمِيَةَ ٱلۡأُنثَىٰ ٢٧\nBecause they do not believe in the Hereafter, they showed audacity in their words and deeds, opposing Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), such as their saying that the angels were the daughters of Allah. Al-Saadi: 820.\nWhat is the reason that induced the polytheists to oppose Allah and His Messenger, and speak falsely about the angels?\nفَأَعۡرِضۡ عَن مَّن تَوَلَّىٰ عَن ذِكۡرِنَا وَلَمۡ يُرِدۡ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا ٢٩\nHaving described their false beliefs and misguidance, Allah commands His Prophet (ﷺ) to turn away from them, as their misguidance was caused by turning their back on Allah’s Message and His remembrance, hence they deserved to be left by turning away from them. Ibn Ashur: 27/116-117.\nThis verse is an example of this saying: The requital befits the action. How?\nوَلَمۡ يُرِدۡ إِلَّا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا ٢٩ ذَٰلِكَ مَبۡلَغُهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِۚ\nMeaning: That is all they know. As for those who believe in the Hereafter, the people of understanding and mature thinking, whose aspirations and goals are focused on the Hereafter, their knowledge is the best and most sublime of knowledge, for it is based on the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 820.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of Islamic knowledge. How?\nذَٰلِكَ مَبۡلَغُهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِۚ\nMeaning: They are well aware of their worldly affairs, but oblivious to their religious affairs. Al-Farra said: Allah belittles and disdains them. Meaning: Preferring this worldly life over the Hereafter showed the narrow extent of their minds and the limited boundary of their knowledge. Al-Qurtubi: 20/41.\nThis verse belittles the disbelievers. How?\nوَإِذۡ أَنتُمۡ أَجِنَّةٞ فِي بُطُونِ أُمَّهَٰتِكُمۡۖ\nMakhūl ibn Ab Muslim (a prominent scholar) said: We were fetuses in our mothers' wombs, and some of us were stillborn, but we remained. Then, we became infants, and some of us died, but we remained. We grew to become young men, and some of us died, but we remained. We became grown men, and some of us died, but we remained, then, we became old men, so after this, what are we waiting for?! Al-Baghawi: 4/261.\nFrom this verse, it is understood that Allah confers great bounty upon us. What is it? What does He call upon us to do?\nفَلَا تُزَكُّوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡۖ هُوَ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَنِ ٱتَّقَىٰٓ ٣٢\nAl-Kalbi and Muqatil said: People used to do good deeds, then they say: Our prayers, fasting, Hajj (pilgrimage), and Jihad, so Allah revealed this verse, (He knows best who is truly righteous), who sincerely obeyed Allah. Al-Baghawi: 4/312.\nWhat is the reason for the revelation of this verse, (do not claim purity for yourselves)?\nوَأَن لَّيۡسَ لِلۡإِنسَٰنِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ٣٩\nThe offspring will be joined with their fathers in the Hereafter, like they were in worldly life. This joining is part of rewarding the fathers for their strive in this life. As for their offspring who will attain this high rank without efforts, it is not meant for them, rather, it is meant for their fathers to make them happier in Paradise by joining them with their offspring. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/82.\nHow do you reconcile these two verses: (And that man will not receive except what he strives for) and (And those who believe and their offspring follow them in faith, We will join with them their offspring)?\nwords\nبِالحُسنَىParadise\nوَالفَوَاحِشَMajor shameful acts\nاللَّمَمَSmall sins that are seldom committed\nوَأَكدَىCeased giving out of stinginess\nأَلاَّ تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌNo bearer of burdens will bear\nوِزرَ أُخرَىThe burden of another\nالمُنتَهَىThe final return for all on the Last Day"],[528,"§An-Najm, Al-Qamar\ndeeds\nListen humbly to recited verses of the Quran.\nWhen reaching the end of Surat Al-Najm, prostrate for recitation.\nConverse with some of your friends about the incident of the moon split asunder.\nguid\nO son of Adam, always remember your weakness, for you are in need of others.\nBelieving in the nearness of the Hour induces one to do righteous deeds.\nFollowing desires prompts a person to deny the truth.\nrefl\nوَقَوۡمَ نُوحٖ مِّن قَبۡلُۖ إِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ هُمۡ أَظۡلَمَ وَأَطۡغَىٰ ٥٢\nOne of the greatest proofs of their wickedness is this verse: (We sent Noah to his people, and he lived among them for a thousand years, less fifty)[29:14]. A people who never responded to the call of a noble and sincere Prophet for all this length of time must be the most transgressing and tyrant among all the people. Al-Tabari: 22/573.\nAllah describes Noah's people as more wicked and rebellious. Why?\nوَأَنتُمۡ سَٰمِدُونَ ٦١\nVain amusements means singing. This interpretation does not contradict what is implied by this verse that vain amusements are heedlessness, since singing contains all that and causes it. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/85-86.\nVain amusements have many interpretations by righteous predecessors. How do reconcile them?\nفَٱسۡجُدُواْۤ لِلَّهِۤ وَٱعۡبُدُواْ۩ ٦٢\nThe command to prostrate to Allah in particular serves to highlight the virtue of this action, which is the core and essence of worship, the core and essence of which is humility before Allah and submission to Him. Prostration is the greatest manifestation of humility and submission, in which a person’s heart and body are in a state of humility, as he places his noblest faculties on the lowly ground, which is the place where feet tread. Al-Saadi: 823.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of prostration. How?\nٱقۡتَرَبَتِ ٱلسَّاعَةُ وَٱنشَقَّ ٱلۡقَمَرُ ١\nThe miracle of the moon splitting asunder was made to remind people about the nearness of the coming of the Hour, where a heavenly body like the moon, which is linked to the earth, went through an extraordinary change. This calls for alerting people to the potential perishing of this world. The past tense is used in this verse to reflect reality. Ibn Ashur: 27/168.\nWhat is the link between (The Hour has come near) and (and the moon has split asunder)?\nٱقۡتَرَبَتِ ٱلسَّاعَةُ\nMeaning: The time for the Day of Resurrection is nearing, which serves as a warning from Allah to His servants that the Day of Resurrection is near and so is the end of this world. Moreover, Allah enjoins His servants to be ready for the horrors of the Day of Resurrection before it comes upon them suddenly while they are heedless. Al-Tabari: 22/565.\nAllah tells His servants about the nearness of the Day of Resurrection. What is the purpose of that?\nوَكَذَّبُواْ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓاْ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡۚ وَكُلُّ أَمۡرٖ مُّسۡتَقِرّٞ ٣\nAl-Qushayri said: When desires are followed, it is considered a bad omen that leads to denial, for Allah confuses the heart of the follower of desires so that he becomes unable to see the right way. In contrast, following the truth is linked to believing, for Allah enlightens the insight of the follower of truth to become a believer. Al-Biqai: 4/312.\nWhat is the outcome of following the desires?\nوَكَذَّبُواْ وَٱتَّبَعُوٓاْ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡۚ وَكُلُّ أَمۡرٖ مُّسۡتَقِرّٞ ٣\nMeaning: The deeds of every person will eventually catch up with him. The righteous deeds will settle the believers in Paradise while evil deeds will settle the disbelievers in the Fire. Al-Qurtubi: 20/75.\nWhat is meant by: (Every matter will reach its inevitable end)?\nwords\nأَغنَى وَأَقنَىHe who enriches and suffices\nالشِّعرَىSirius, a star worshiped by some pagans\nوَالمُؤتَفِكَةَThe toppled cities of the people of Lot (u)\nأَهوَىHe hurled the cities down after lifting them\nفَغَشَّاهَاCovered by stones\nتَتَمَارَىYou doubt"],[529,"§Al-Qamar\ndeeds\nInvoke Allah to relieve your hardship.\nSelect a verse or more and reflect on their lessons and aims.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nguid\nAllah has protected and helped His Prophet Noah (u).\nAllah has punished those who disobeyed and transgressed.\nTesting the Prophets and their followers is part of Allah's ways.\nrefl\nخُشَّعًا أَبۡصَٰرُهُمۡ يَخۡرُجُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡأَجۡدَاثِ كَأَنَّهُمۡ جَرَادٞ مُّنتَشِرٞ ٧\nHumbleness of the eyes indicates submissiveness and humiliation. Humbleness is attributed to the eyes because pride and humiliation are reflected in a man's eyes. Allah says, (Their eyes humbled)[79:9], and He says, (Humbled from humiliation, looking from [behind] a covert glance)[42:45]. Al-Qurtubi: 20/78.\nHumbleness is attributed to the eyes. Why?\nيَقُولُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ هَٰذَا يَوۡمٌ عَسِرٞ ٨\nWhat this implies is that it will be easy for the believers. Al-Saadi: 825.\nWhat is inferred from knowing that the Day of Resurrection will be hard for the disbelievers?\nفَدَعَا رَبَّهُۥٓ أَنِّي مَغۡلُوبٞ فَٱنتَصِرۡ ١٠\nMeaning: I am weak and cannot overcome or resist my people, so help Your religion. Ibn Kathir: 4/265.\nThis verse indicates the importance of supplication while preaching. Explain.\nوَلَقَدۡ يَسَّرۡنَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِلذِّكۡرِ فَهَلۡ مِن مُّدَّكِرٖ ١٧\nAl-Qushayri said: Allah made the Quran recitation easy for some, eased its learning for others, eased its understanding for some, and eased its memorization for others. They are all the people of the Quran, the people of Allah and those who are closest to Him. Al-Biqai: 19/108.\nDescribe how the Quran is made easy in many aspects.\nوَلَقَدۡ يَسَّرۡنَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِلذِّكۡرِ فَهَلۡ مِن مُّدَّكِرٖ ١٧\nMeaning: We have made the Quran easy to memorize. This is known by observation because unlike other books, children can memorize it perfectly. It is said that none of the Books sent down by Allah was memorized except the Quran. Moreover, it is said that the meaning of this verse is: We made the Quran easy to understand and by which to be admonished because it contains proof and eloquent wisdom. Ibn Juzay: 2/389.\nAllah made the Quran easy for remembrance. How?\nفَكَيۡفَ كَانَ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ ١٦\nThis eloquent verse is repeated, and this one, (So taste My punishment and warning) to warn the listener at every story so that he takes heed, for there is a lesson and admonishment in each one of them, hence, He concludes each story by warning the listener of the threat. Ibn Juzay: 2/389.\nAllah repeats this verse, (And how [severe] were My punishment and warning). Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ يَسَّرۡنَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِلذِّكۡرِ فَهَلۡ مِن مُّدَّكِرٖ ١٧\nPraise be to Allah, the easiest thing for souls to learn, memorize, and understand is the Book of Allah, Who made it easy for remembrance. What is really hard is the misinterpretation of minds, and the false arguments over fundamentals and incidentals for which Allah has not sent down any authority. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/87.\nWhat is the easiest source for knowledge and practice?\nwords\nخُشَّعًاHumbled by fear\nالأَجدَاثِGraves\nمُهطِعِينَRushing ahead\nوَازدُجِرَHe was repelled and threatened\nمُنهَمِرٍPouring down\nقُدِرَPredestined\nعَلَى ذَاتِ أَلوَاحٍ وَدُسُرٍAn Ark made of planks and nails\nمُدَّكِرٍOne who takes heed\nيَومِ نَحسٍA day of continuous misfortune"],[530,"§Al-Qamar\ndeeds\nThank Allah for His blessings upon you in words and in deeds, and draw closer to Him by performing a righteous deed.\nDraw two useful lessons from reading the verses on this page.\nConverse with someone about the horrors of Hellfire, or write an article about them.\nguid\nThose who deny and disobey must be wary of Allah's punishment.\nBe certain of Allah's promise and help.\nBelieving in divine will and destiny is an essential part of faith.\nrefl\nفَنَادَوۡاْ صَاحِبَهُمۡ فَتَعَاطَىٰ فَعَقَرَ ٢٩\nHe is referred to as (their companion) to indicate that they were content with his action; they were allied with him and supportive. Ibn Ashur: 27/201.\nPeople of Thamūd consented to the action of the one who hamstrung the she-camel. What is the evidence for that?\nإِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ حَاصِبًا إِلَّآ ءَالَ لُوطٖۖ نَّجَّيۡنَٰهُم بِسَحَرٖ ٣٤ نِّعۡمَةٗ مِّنۡ عِندِنَاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي مَن شَكَرَ ٣٥\nAl-Qushayri said: Giving thanks to Allah for the blessings of protection [safety] is more complete than giving thanks to Him for the blessings of benefits. This is known only to those who are successful and prudent. Al-Biqai: 19/125.\nWhat are the types of blessings? Which ones are more deserving to thank Allah for?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَنذَرَهُم بَطۡشَتَنَا فَتَمَارَوۡاْ بِٱلنُّذُرِ ٣٦\n(Our assault), Our punishing seizure commensurate with Our Might. (Our assault) is in singular form to indicate that none of Allah's punishments should be taken lightly, rather, a single seizure by Him is more than enough, and no second one is needed. Al-Biqai: 19/125.\n(Our assault) is in singular form. Why?\nفَذُوقُواْ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ ٣٧\nThey were specially commanded to (taste) due to their pleasure in their shameful act. Al-Biqai: 19/113\nThe story of the people of Lot (u) ends with (So taste My punishment and warning). Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ وَسُعُرٖ ٤٧\n(Indeed, the criminals), those who committed many evil deeds and grave sins, such as associating partners with Allah and other acts of disobedience (are in error and torment), they are misguided in this world, straying from knowledge and straying from righteous deeds that could save them from divine punishment, and on the Day of Resurrection, they will find themselves suffering a painful punishment. Al-Saadi: 827.\nDescribe two acts of misguidance by criminals in this worldly life.\nيَوۡمَ يُسۡحَبُونَ فِي ٱلنَّارِ عَلَىٰ وُجُوهِهِمۡ\nThe face is the noblest part of the body, where pain is felt more intensely than pain elsewhere in the body. Thus, they will be humiliated and disgraced. Al-Saadi: 828.\nAllah's way of punishing the criminals has physical and mental pains. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nشِربٍA share of water\nفَتَعَاطَىHe took the she-camel with his hands\nفَعَقَرَHe hamstrung\nكَهَشِيمِ المُحتَظِرِDry twig fragments of an animal pen\nحَاصِبًاA storm of stones\nفَتَمَارَواThey doubted and denied\nأَدهَى وَأَمَرُّMore disastrous and more bitter than what they faced in the Battle of Badr\nوَسُعُرٍTorment"],[531,"§Al-Qamar, Ar-Rahman\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask you for Paradise, its bliss, and those words and deeds that bring me closer to it .\"\nThank Allah for teaching you the Quran.\nRemember a great blessing for which Allah selected you, then thank Him for it.\nguid\nLearning the Holy Quran leads to eloquence and good speech.\nThe heavens and earth were based upon justice of which the balance is one of its means.\nThanking Allah for His countless favors is an essential part of the faith.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ أَهۡلَكۡنَآ أَشۡيَاعَكُمۡ فَهَلۡ مِن مُّدَّكِرٖ ٥١\n((And We have destroyed many like you) of the previous nations who did deeds such as you have done, and disbelieved as you have disbelieved. (Is there anyone to take heed), is there anyone who will pay heed and realize that Allah's way of dealing with the earlier and later generations is the same, and that just as His wisdom decreed that the earlier evildoers be destroyed, these people are just like them, and there is no difference between the two groups. Al-Saadi: 828.\nAllah relates to us the destruction of past nations. Why?\nفِي مَقۡعَدِ صِدۡقٍ عِندَ مَلِيكٖ مُّقۡتَدِرِۢ ٥٥\n(The Most Powerful), He possesses infinite powers beyond which what others can comprehend. He provides the righteous with every good and protects them from every harm. This holy name, (the Most Powerful) is the key to overpowering the transgressors. Al-Biqai: 19/137.\nWhat does this holy name (The Most Powerful) indicate?\nفِي مَقۡعَدِ صِدۡقٍ عِندَ مَلِيكٖ مُّقۡتَدِرِۢ ٥٥\nJa'far Al-Sadiq said: Allah praises the seat of truth in which only truthful people sit. Al-Qurtubi: 20/109.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of truthfulness. How?\nٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ ١ عَلَّمَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ ٢ خَلَقَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ ٣ عَلَّمَهُ ٱلۡبَيَانَ ٤\nAfter mentioning the favor of teaching the Quran, Allah mentions the creation of man because it is the basis upon which all favors are bestowed. The mention of teaching the Quran precedes all favors because it is the greatest of them all. Al-Alusi: 14/99.\nThe mention of teaching the Quran precedes all favors. Why?\nعَلَّمَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ ٢\nSince this Surah enumerates Allah's favors upon His servants, Allah begins with the greatest favor, the most useful, and has the greatest return of them all, which is the favor of teaching the Quran, as it is it leads to happiness in this life and the Hereafter, brings the good of both, and guides to the best in them. Al-Shawkani: 5/131.\nSurat Ar-Rahman begins by mentioning the teaching of the Quran. Why?\nوَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلۡوَزۡنَ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِ وَلَا تُخۡسِرُواْ ٱلۡمِيزَانَ ٩\nQatadah said: O son of Adam, be fair to others as you wish to be dealt with fairness, and fulfill your commitments as you like to have the same done to you, as the righteousness of people is established through justice. Al-Qurtubi: 20/118.\nThis verse contains guidance, what is it?\nوَمَآ أَمۡرُنَآ إِلَّا وَٰحِدَةٞ كَلَمۡحِۢ بِٱلۡبَصَرِ ٥٠\n(And Our command is but one), only once. (Like a glance of the eye), means that Allah's decree upon His creations is faster than a glance of the eye. A glance is a swift look. Al-Baghawi: 20/107.\nFrom your reading of this Surah, give an example of Allah’s swift decree upon denying nations.\nخَلَقَ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِن صَلۡصَٰلٖ كَٱلۡفَخَّارِ ١٤ وَخَلَقَ ٱلۡجَآنَّ مِن مَّارِجٖ مِّن نَّارٖ ١٥\nThis is indicative of the noble nature of the essence of the human being who is created from clay and dust, which has the characteristics of stability, gravity, and usefulness, in contrast to the essence of the jinn, namely fire, which has the characteristics of immaturity, foolishness, evil and mischief. Al-Saadi: 829.\nThis verse indicates the virtue of man in comparison to the jinn. How?\nwords\nإِلاَّ وَاحِدَةٌA single word, which is: \"Be\"\nمُستَطَرٌWritten down in their records of deeds\nمَقعَدِ صِدقٍA seat of honor with no idle talk or sinful speech\nبِحُسبَانٍThey move by precise calculation\nوَضَعَهَا لِلأَنَامِHe laid out the earth for all creatures\nالأَكمَامِSheaths that contain fruits\nوَالحَبُّ ذُو العَصفِA grain having husks\nصَلصَالٍA dry clay\nكَالفَخَّارِLike pottery"],[532,"§Ar-Rahman\ndeeds\nRemember the last five of your deceased relatives and ask for Allah's mercy on them.\nReflect on the greatness of Allah when reading the meaning of this verse,\nRecall a sin you committed, then give to charity so that Allah may forgive you.\nguid\nAll created beings are in need of Allah.\nBeing fearful and in awe of Allah is very important.\nRemind yourself of the horrors of the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nكُلُّ مَنۡ عَلَيۡهَا فَانٍ ٢٦\n(To Him belong the sailing ships raised up in the sea like mountains), Allah mentions His blessing of creating the means for surviving disasters and establishing livelihood for people by making available for them sailing ships for their travel in safety. Describing the ships as mountains indicates the expansion of this blessing. Then Allah reminds the people that all of that will not prevent His decree that they are all destined to perish. Ibn Ashur: 27/252.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the ones before it?\nكُلَّ يَوۡمٍ هُوَ فِي شَأۡنٖ ٢٩\nIt was narrated from Abu Darda' that the Prophet said: \"His affairs include forgiving sins, relieving distress, raising some people and bringing others low.\" Al-Qurtubi: 20/134.\nWhat is meant by (Every day He is engaged in some matters)?\nسَنَفۡرُغُ لَكُمۡ أَيُّهَ ٱلثَّقَلَانِ ٣١\nAttending to them does not indicate that Allah was busy with something before that because He can never be distracted by anything, but, here, Allah is threatening men and jinn with reckoning. Al-Baghawi: 4/492.\nWhat is meant by (We will attend to you, O prominent beings)?\nسَنَفۡرُغُ لَكُمۡ أَيُّهَ ٱلثَّقَلَانِ ٣١\nJinn and men are called (prominent beings) due to their importance among the inhabitants of the earth. Moreover, it is said that they are called as such because of their burden on earth in life and death, as described by this verse: (And the earth throws out its burdens)[99:2]. Ja'far Al-Sadiq said: They are called as such because they are burdened by sins. Al-Shawkani: 5/137.\nThe jinn and men are called (prominent beings). Why?\nيُرۡسَلُ عَلَيۡكُمَا شُوَاظٞ مِّن نَّارٖ وَنُحَاسٞ فَلَا تَنتَصِرَانِ ٣٥ فَبِأَيِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ ٣٦\nMeaning: He will send against you pure flames of fire (and smoke). What is meant is that these two frightening things will be sent against you, O jinn and humans, and they will encompass you, then you will not be able to protect yourselves and no one will protect you against Allah. Because His alarming His servants is a blessing to them and a motive that should push them toward the most sublime aims, Allah reminds them of His blessings, saying: (Then which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?). Al-Saadi: 831.\nThe mention of the Fire is a blessing for the believers. How?\nفَإِذَا ٱنشَقَّتِ ٱلسَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتۡ وَرۡدَةٗ كَٱلدِّهَانِ ٣٧\nThe heaven is likened to oil on the Day of Resurrection because it will melt due to the horrors of that Day. Moreover, it is said that the heaven will shine similar to the shine of oil. It is, also, said that oil means reddish skin. Ibn Juzay: 2/395.\nThe heaven is, eloquently, likened to oil. Explain.\nفَيَوۡمَئِذٖ لَّا يُسۡـَٔلُ عَن ذَنۢبِهِۦٓ إِنسٞ وَلَا جَآنّٞ ٣٩\nThis verse describes one scene on the Day of Resurrection while this verse: (By your Lord, We will surely question them all)[15:92] describes another scene. Moreover, it is said that they will not be asked for information about their sins because Allah, the Almighty, has kept complete records of His servants’ deeds, rather, they will be censured and rebuked. Al-Shawkani: 5/138.\nHow do we reconcile this verse and: (By your Lord, We will surely question them all)?\nwords\nمَرَجَ البَحرَينِTwo bodies of water: Fresh and salty\nبَرزَخٌA barrier\nالجَوَارِHuge sailing ships\nفَانٍPerishes\nفِي شَأنٍA matter such as giving life and causing death, enriching some and impoverishing others, elevating some and debasing others\nتَنفُذُواFinding a pass for escape\nشُوَاظٌA flame of fire\nكَالدِّهَانِA rose-colored like oil, or a red skin\nبِسِيمَاهُمBy their marks"],[533,"§Ar-Rahman\ndeeds\nDo a good deed that reflects your fear of Allah, the Almighty.\nCoverse with a friend about Hellfire, or write an article in which you describe its horrors and your belief in it.\nRecall someone who has done good to you, then say to him: \"May Allah reward you good\"; and if you can gift him, it would be good.\nguid\nAsk refuge with Allah from the torment of Hellfire.\nBeing fearful of Allah, the Almighty, is very important.\nAllah's bounty, generosity, and mercy toward His servants are limitless.\nrefl\nهَٰذِهِۦ جَهَنَّمُ ٱلَّتِي يُكَذِّبُ بِهَا ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ ٤٣ يَطُوفُونَ بَيۡنَهَا وَبَيۡنَ حَمِيمٍ ءَانٖ ٤٤ فَبِأَيِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ ٤٥\nPunishing disobedient criminals as well as honoring those who fear Allah, is from His grace, mercy, justice, compassion and kindness for His creatures. His warnings against His torment and punishment, such as mentioned in these verses, should encourage people to abandon the Shirk and disobedience they engage in. That is why Allah reminds them of this favor, (So which of the favors of your Lord would you deny?). Ibn Kathir: 4/278.\nAllah mentions the punishment of the criminals in the Fire, then He reminds them of this favor (So which of the favors of your Lord would you deny). How?\nوَلِمَنۡ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهِۦ جَنَّتَانِ ٤٦\nAr-Raghib says: Fear of Allah is not like what would one feel when facing a lion, rather, it means refraining from sins and pursuing good deeds. That is why it is said that whoever does not abandon sins, does not fear Allah. Al-Alusi: 14/115.\nHow does one fear the position of Allah?\nمُتَّكِـِٔينَ عَلَىٰ فُرُشِۢ بَطَآئِنُهَا مِنۡ إِسۡتَبۡرَقٖۚ\nNo one knows the description and beauty of those beds except Allah, even their linings that touch the ground directly will be made of brocade, which is the most beautiful and finest kind of silk, so how about the tops of those beds that will be in contact with people’s skin? Al-Saadi: 831.\nWhat is the indication of the beauty of the beds' linings?\nوَجَنَى ٱلۡجَنَّتَيۡنِ دَانٖ ٥٤\nIn paradise, the fruit is near for handpicking at any position a person may be: Standing, sitting, or lying down because in all cases, the fruit will hang low for him. Ibn Juzay: 2/396.\nThe fruit of Paradise is hanging low. Explain.\nكَأَنَّهُنَّ ٱلۡيَاقُوتُ وَٱلۡمَرۡجَانُ ٥٨\nThe women in Paradise are likened to the rubies and coral due to the reddish color of their cheeks, similar to likening cheeks to red roses. Moreover, sometimes, white color is called red, as in the Prophetic Hadith: \"I have been sent to all the red and the black.\" Ibn Ashur: 27/270.\nThe women in Paradise are likened to the rubies and coral. Why?\nهَلۡ جَزَآءُ ٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنِ إِلَّا ٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنُ ٦٠\nMeaning: Whoever does good by obeying Allah, Allah will reward him with Paradise. Moreover, doing good may mean what was described by the Prophet (ﷺ) when the angel Gabriel asked him, and he replied: \"It is to worship Allah as if you are seeing Him; and although you do not see Him, He sees you.\" This is the stage of being conscious of Allah’s presence in one’s life. So, Allah makes these two gardens a reward for the foremost doers of good, and He makes another two gardens, which are lesser than the first ones, for those who are ordinary doers of good. Ibn Juzay: 2/396.\nWhat is meant by the two words of (good) in this verse?\nهَلۡ جَزَآءُ ٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنِ إِلَّا ٱلۡإِحۡسَٰنُ ٦٠\nAllah says concerning the first two gardens: (Is the reward for good [anything] but good?) [55:60], which indicates that the first two gardens are the reward for the foremost doers of good, and He does not say that concerning the second two gardens. From the points mentioned above, we may conclude that the first two gardens are superior to the second two gardens, and that they are prepared for those who are close to Allah, namely the Prophets, the people of truth, and the elite among the righteous servants of Allah, and that the second two are prepared for the ordinary believers. Al-Saadi: 832.\nAllah says, concerning the first two gardens: (Is the reward for good [anything] but good?), but does not say the same for the second two gardens. Why?\nwords\nحَمِيمٍ آنٍScalding water\nبَطَائِنُهَاLinings\nإِستَبرَقٍSilk brocade\nدانHanging low\nقَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرفِLimiting their glances to their husbands\nيَطمِثهُنَّUntouched by men\nمُدهَآمَّتَانِDark green in color\nنَضَّاخَتَانِTwo gushing springs"],[534,"§Al-Waqi'ah, Ar-Rahman\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to raise your rank in the Hereafter.\nBe the first comer to the mosque today for one of the five daily prayers.\nBe the first one among your brothers to kiss the heads of your parents today.\nguid\nThe horrors of the Day of Resurrection are immense.\nBeing in the forefront of doing good is a virtue.\nThe reward fits the deed.\nrefl\nحُورٞ مَّقۡصُورَٰتٞ فِي ٱلۡخِيَامِ ٧٢\nBeautiful fair women reserved, and guarded because women are praised for staying in their houses, and censured for leaving them. Ibn Juzay: 2/397.\nExplain how this verse encourages women to stay in their houses.\nإِذَا وَقَعَتِ ٱلۡوَاقِعَةُ ١\nIt is called Waqi'ah because its occurrence is inevitable, or because it is very near. Moreover, it may be because of its immense hardships. Al-Shawkani: 5/147.\nWhy is Al-Waqi'ah called as such?\nخَافِضَةٞ رَّافِعَةٌ ٣\nIt will bring some people down to the Fire and raise others to Paradise. Ibn Abbas (k) said: It will bring down some people who, in this life, were in high places, and will raise others who, in this life, were oppressed. Al-Baghawi: 4/301.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, who will be brought down, and who will be raised?\nوَالسّٰبِقُوْنَ السّٰبِقُوْنَ ١٠\nThose who rush to obey Allah in this life and are foremost in performing acts of righteousness, will be among the foremost believers honored in the Hereafter. Verily, the reward fits the deed. Ibn Kathir: 4/285.\nWhy will these people be the forerunners in the Hereafter?\nثُلَّةٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ١٣ وَقَلِيلٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡأٓخِرِينَ ١٤\n(Many from the early generations), many from the earlier generations of this Ummah and other nations. (And a few from the later generations): This is indicative of the superiority of the early generations of this Ummah over its later generations, in general terms, because the numbers of those who were close to Allah are greater among the earlier generations than among the later generations. Al-Saadi: 833.\nThese two verses indicate the superiority of earlier generations of this Ummah over its later ones. Explain.\nعَلَىٰ سُرُرٖ مَّوۡضُونَةٖ ١٥ مُّتَّكِـِٔينَ عَلَيۡهَا مُتَقَٰبِلِينَ ١٦\nIn any large gathering of people, some will inevitably have their backs toward others. But, the gatherings in Paradise will be different. He says, (Facing each other), without being distant, or facing the backs of one another, or disliking each other. Al-Biqai: 19/203.\nWhat is meant by (facing each other)?\nمُّتَّكِـِٔينَ عَلَيۡهَا مُتَقَٰبِلِينَ ١٦\nFacing one another because of their purity of heart and good manners, and the harmony among them. Al-Saadi: 833.\nThis verse indicates the purity of the hearts of the people of Paradise, and the removal of resentment and ill feeling from their hearts. Explain.\nwords\nخَيرَاتٌGood and beautiful wives\nحُورٌFair beautiful women\nمَقصُورَاتٌReserved and guarded\nيَطمِثهُنَّUntouched by men\nرَفرَفٍ خُضرGreen cushions\nوَعَبقَرِيٍّSplendid carpets\nرُجَّتِShaken\nوَبُسَّتِCrushed\nثُلَّةٌA multitude\nمَوضُونَةٍWoven with gold"],[535,"§Al-Waqi'ah\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to be among the people of the right.\nGive some fruit or meat to a needy person so that you may attain the fruit and meat of Paradise.\nAbstain from a luxurious side in your life for a day.\nguid\nThe wife's devotion and love for her husband is one of the reasons for family stability.\nAllah prepared a great reward in the Hereafter for His servants for their patience and obedience in this worldly life.\nKeep away from the traits of the people of the left, and seek refuge with Allah from them.\nrefl\nوَفَٰكِهَةٖ مِّمَّا يَتَخَيَّرُونَ ٢٠ وَلَحۡمِ طَيۡرٖ مِّمَّا يَشۡتَهُونَ ٢١\nWhen eating , staring with fruits is a medically sound advice because they are lighter, easier to swallow, and take less time to digest. It is stated that one of the reasons for catching Cholera (infectious diarrhea) is eating lighter food after a heavy meal. Al-Alusi: 14/137.\nFruit is mentioned before meat. Why?\nوَحُورٌ عِينٞ ٢٢ كَأَمۡثَٰلِ ٱللُّؤۡلُوِٕ ٱلۡمَكۡنُونِ ٢٣\nHe likens them to pearls in whiteness, and describes the pearls as preserved to indicate their permanent beauty. Ibn Juzay: 2/400.\nThe women in Paradise are likened to preserved pearls. Why?\nوَظِلّٖ مَّمۡدُودٖ ٣٠\nMeaning: An extended permanent shade because it does not change by the sun. Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"In Paradise, there is a tree under the shadow of which a rider can travel for a hundred years without passing it; if you wish, you can recite: (And extended shade).\" Ibn Juzay: 2/401.\nFrom the Prophetic interpretation, state an example of the extended shade on the Day of Resurrection.\nلَّا مَقۡطُوعَةٖ وَلَا مَمۡنُوعَةٖ ٣٣\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"It will not cease when picked, and it will not be kept from anyone who wants it.\" Some said:\"It will not cease with time, and it will not be kept away by high price, similar to what is done in worldly life when most fruits are restricted during winter except for high prices.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/306.\nWhat is meant by (Neither ceasing nor restricted)?\nعُرُبًا أَتۡرَابٗا ٣٧\nIn the Arabic text, (Uruban), which means extremely loving and devoted wives to their husbands. Al-Shawkani: 5/153.\nWhat is meant by (Uruban)?\nوَظِلّٖ مِّن يَحۡمُومٖ ٤٣ لَّا بَارِدٖ وَلَا كَرِيمٍ ٤٤\nMeaning: There will be distress, anguish, grief and suffering in which there is nothing good, because negation of a thing is an affirmation of its opposite. Al-Saadi: 834.\nWhat is meant by (Neither cool nor beneficial)?\nإِنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ قَبۡلَ ذَٰلِكَ مُتۡرَفِينَ ٤٥\nThe people of the left [disbelievers] are described as living in luxuries since almost all of them enjoy the blessings of eating, drinking, and women. Moreover, they limited their thinking to worldly pleasures, which kept them from reflecting on the truth to which the Messenger (ﷺ) used to call them. Living in luxuries was one of the reasons for their mentioned punishment. Ibn Ashur: 27/306.\nLiving in luxuries can be risky and punishable in the Hereafter. Explain.\nwords\nلاَ يُصَدَّعُونَ عَنهَاNo headache will they have therefrom\nوَلاَ يُنزِفُونَNor will they be intoxicated\nالمَكنُونِPearls well-protected\nسِدرٍ مَخضُودٍThornless lote trees\nوَطَلحٍ مَنضُودٍClusters of bananas, or at-Talh tree\nعُرُبًاLoving their husband\nأَترَابًاOf equal age"],[536,"§Al-Waqi'ah\ndeeds\nWhen you eat, think about the stages through which this food went until it became ready for eating, then thank Allah for that.\nPraise Allah whenever you drink water.\nWhen you bow, reflect on this verse and say, \"Glorified is my Lord the Great.\"\nguid\nSubmitting to Allah for His blessings upon us in creating, providing provision, and governing all affairs.\nFire is useful to people in their worldly affairs and it is, also, a reminder of Hellfire in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nنَحۡنُ قَدَّرۡنَا بَيۡنَكُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ وَمَا نَحۡنُ بِمَسۡبُوقِينَ ٦٠\nMeaning: We ordained death at the end of a prescribed lifetime for everyone, where he cannot live beyond his prescribed limit. We may ordain a short lifetime for one who has a strong body and sound mind, and We may ordain a long lifetime for one who has a weak body and unsteady mind. You admit that Allah governs all actions in accordance with the utmost perfection, capability, and extensive wisdom. Al-Biqai: 19/221.\nWhat is meant by (We have decreed death among you)?\nوَلَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتُمُ ٱلنَّشۡأَةَ ٱلۡأُولَىٰ فَلَوۡلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٦٢\n(So will you not remember), Allah says: O people, will you remember and realize that the One Who created you the first time when you were nothing is quite capable of bringing you back to life after death. Al-Tabari: 23/138.\nAllah links reminding to the first creation. Why?\nءَأَنتُمۡ تَزۡرَعُونَهُۥٓ أَمۡ نَحۡنُ ٱلزَّٰرِعُونَ ٦٤\nThis verse contains two points, first: Allah reminds them of His favor in growing their crops to keep them alive so they would thank Him for His blessing. Second: Allah presents evidence to be considered, which is growing their crops after its seed has perished in the soil and transformed into green crops, then making it stronger than ever before, is even more capable of bringing people from the dead. In this, a compelling proof to those of sensible minds. Al-Qurtubi: 20/211.\nIn brief, discuss Allah's favor upon His servants in growing their crops.\nأَفَرَءَيۡتُمُ ٱلۡمَآءَ ٱلَّذِي تَشۡرَبُونَ ٦٨\nAmong many water benefits, Allah mentions only one, which is drinking because it is the greatest and most beneficial of all. Al-Shawkani: 5/158.\nAmong many benefits of water, Allah mentions only one. Why?\nأَفَرَءَيۡتُمُ ٱلۡمَآءَ ٱلَّذِي تَشۡرَبُونَ ٦٨ ءَأَنتُمۡ أَنزَلۡتُمُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُزۡنِ أَمۡ نَحۡنُ ٱلۡمُنزِلُونَ ٦٩\n(Is it you who bring it down from the clouds), indicates that all ground waters that flow out of springs and wells, are originated from the clouds and Allah settled and stored it in the earth for His creations. Al-Shanqiti: 7/534.\nFrom where do the ground waters of springs and wells originate?\nنَحۡنُ جَعَلۡنَٰهَا تَذۡكِرَةٗ وَمَتَٰعٗا لِّلۡمُقۡوِينَ ٧٣\nAllah singles out travelers for mention because they benefit from it more than others. Perhaps the reason for that is that this world is all a place of travel; from the time a person is born, he is traveling toward his Lord. Al-Saadi: 835-836.\nAllah singles out travelers for mention of benefiting from the fire. Why?\nفَسَبِّحۡ بِٱسۡمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٧٤\nExalting and glorifying Allah, the Almighty, after mentioning His blessings indicates praising Him for them. It is, in fact, offering thanks to the Bestower. Al-Alusi: 14/15\nIn this verse, what is the indication of glorifying Allah after mentioning His blessings?\nwords\nزَقُّومٍThe tree of Zaqqum\nشُربَ الهِيمِDrinking like thirsty camels do\nبِمَسبُوقِينَOutdone\nتَفَكَّهُونَWondering about what happened\nإِنَّا لَمُغرَمُونَWe suffered loss\nالمُزنِClouds\nأُجَاجًاSalty useless water\nتُورُونَYou kindle"],[537,"§Al-Waqi'ah, Al-Hadid\ndeeds\nAlways show respect when handling the Book of Allah by placing it properly on the shelves at your mosque and keeping it clean.\nVisit a patient, a place for washing and preparing the dead, or a cemetery.\nPerform ablution before reciting the Quran.\nguid\nMaking concessions to the enemies of Allah despite their evident disbelief and denial of the revelation is considered a sort of denial.\nThose who are brought near to Allah will have great rewards.\nBe keen to learn the Holy Names of Allah and invoke Him by them.\nrefl\nإِنَّهُۥ لَقُرۡءَانٞ كَرِيمٞ ٧٧\nMeaning: Allah has honored the Quran and raised it above all previous books. He protected it from containing magic, conjecture, or falsehood. It is said that it is called (noble) because it enjoins good morals and high standards. Moreover, it is said that is because it honors those who memorize it, and elevates those who recite it. Al-Wahidi reported this explanation by those who work with semantics: Describing the Holy Quran as (noble) because it leads to abundance of good by its signs and proofs that show the truth of religion. Al-Azhari said: Noble is a comprehensive name for everything that is praised, and the Holy Quran is praised for its guidance, clarification, knowledge, and wisdom. Al-Shawkani: 5/160.\nState some of the honors of the Quran.\nإِنَّهُۥ لَقُرۡءَانٞ كَرِيمٞ ٧٧ فِي كِتَٰبٖ مَّكۡنُونٖ ٧٨ لَّا يَمَسُّهُۥٓ إِلَّا ٱلۡمُطَهَّرُونَ ٧٩\nThis verse, through its allusion, indicates that no one will be able to grasp the meanings of the Quran, nor understand it except those with pure hearts. It is forbidden for those with impure hearts that are filled with religious innovations and oppositions to attain its meanings or understand it. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/120.\nWhoever seeks to understand the Quran, must purify his heart. Explain.\nتَنزِيلٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٨٠\nAllah attributes the revelation of the Quran to His Lordship of the worlds. His Lordship entails His ownership, sovereignty, and rule over them. With all that, it is inconceivable for His complete lordship of them to leave them neglected, create them with no purpose, does not enjoin nor forbid them, and does not reward nor punish them. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/121.\nAllah attributes the revelation of the Quran to His Lordship. Why?\nتَنزِيلٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٨٠\nMeaning: This Quran which is described in these sublime terms is a revelation from the Lord of the worlds, Who takes care of His servants by bestowing His blessings, both spiritual and worldly. One of the most important aspects of caring for His servants is the revelation of this Quran, which guides to what is in the best interests of people in both realms. Al-Saadi: 836.\nAfter mentioning the revelation of the Quran, Allah describes Himself as the Lord of the worlds. Why?\nأَفَبِهَٰذَا ٱلۡحَدِيثِ أَنتُم مُّدۡهِنُونَ ٨١\nMeaning: O people, do you use this Quran, about which I informed and explained to you, to make concessions to the disbelievers, which would entice them to persist in their denial and disbelief in it. Al-Tabari: 23/152.\nWhat is meant by: (Do you take this discourse lightly)?\nوَتَجۡعَلُونَ رِزۡقَكُمۡ أَنَّكُمۡ تُكَذِّبُونَ ٨٢\nIbn Atiyah said: The interpreters unanimously agreed that this verse is a rebuke to those who, when it rains, say: We have been given rain by such and such a star. Meaning: Instead of thanking Allah for the provision He gives you, you deny Him. Ibn Juzay: 2/406.\nIn this verse, what is meant by: (provision) and (deny)?\nهُوَ ٱلۡأَوَّلُ وَٱلۡأٓخِرُ وَٱلظَّٰهِرُ وَٱلۡبَاطِنُۖ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٌ ٣\nMeaning: Allah is the (First) before everything, Who has no beginning, and He was and nothing else existed before Him. (The Last) after everything perishes; He endures eternally when nothing else remains. (The Most High): The victor, the highest above all things. (The Most Near): The All-Knower of everything. That is the meaning of the saying of Ibn Abbas (k). Al-Baghawi: 4/322.\nExplain the meaning of above-mentioned holy names of Allah.\nwords\nمَكنُونٍPreserved, well-protected\nمُدهِنُونَYou deny\nغَيرَ مَدِينِينِExempted from reckoning, recompense\nفَرَوحٌVast mercy, rest, delight\nفَنُزُلٌAccommodation\nالأَوَّلُOne Whom nothing is before Him\nوَالآخِرُOne Whom nothing is after Him\nوَالظَّاهِرُOne Whom nothing is above Him\nوَالبَاطِنُOne Whom nothing is nearer than Him"],[538,"§Al-Hadid\ndeeds\nDraw two useful lessons from this verse:\nSpend some of your wealth while being aware that Allah has entrusted you with it.\nExplain a verse from the Quran to a Muslim who needs to know its meaning.\nguid\nThis is a reminder of Allah's greatness.\nThe believer should not be heedless of the fact that Allah is with him by means of His knowledge and that He is well aware of him.\nRemember the great reward that is attained by one who spends his wealth in the cause of Allah.\nrefl\nوَهُوَ مَعَكُمۡ أَيۡنَ مَا كُنتُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٞ ٤\nThis \"being with\" means that Allah is with them by means of His knowledge and His being aware of them. Hence, He issues a warning and a promise to them of requital for deeds by saying: (And Allah is All-Seeing of what you do). Al-Saadi: 838.\nWhat is meant by (He is with you) in this verse?\nءَامِنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَأَنفِقُواْ مِمَّا جَعَلَكُم مُّسۡتَخۡلَفِينَ فِيهِۖ فَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مِنكُمۡ وَأَنفَقُواْ لَهُمۡ أَجۡرٞ كَبِيرٞ ٧\n(Entrusted you with), the wealth that you have belongs to Allah because He created it, but He made you successive inheritors in managing it like agents, so do not cease spending it in which its real owner enjoined you. Ibn Juzay: 2/410.\nThis verse (Entrusted you with) indicates an important fact. What is it?\nوَمَا لَكُمۡ أَلَّا تُنفِقُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَلِلَّهِ مِيرَٰثُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ\nMeaning: Spend and do not fear poverty or scarcity. Surely, He in Whose cause you spent is the King and Owner of the heavens, and the keys of the heavens and earth are in His Hand, including their treasuries. Ibn Kathir: 4/307.\nAfter enjoining spending in His cause, Allah says, (to Allah belongs the heritage of the heavens and the earth). Why?\nلَا يَسۡتَوِي مِنكُم مَّنۡ أَنفَقَ مِن قَبۡلِ ٱلۡفَتۡحِ\nSpending before the conquest of Makkah was greater [in reward] because people’s needs were greater due to the weakness of Muslims, and spending was much harder for those who did, thus, the reward fits the hardship. Al-Qurtubi: 20/240.\nSpending before the conquest of Makkah was greater in reward. Why?\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يُقۡرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا فَيُضَٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥ وَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٞ كَرِيمٞ ١١\nIn the Quran, the mention of the loan is described as goodly because it combines three things, first: It comes out of good and lawful earnings, not bad or unlawful sources. Second: The spender gives it in good and firm spirit seeking Allah's pleasure. Third: He gives it without reminders of generosity or hurtful words. So, the first thing is related to the money, the second is related to the spender's relation with Allah, and the third is related to the spender's relation with the taker. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/128.\nWhen is a charity described as a goodly loan?\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يُقۡرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا فَيُضَٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥ وَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٞ كَرِيمٞ ١١\nThis spending is called a goodly loan to encourage the souls to spend in the cause of Allah because when the spender knows that he is dealing with Allah, the Rich and Bountiful, spending becomes easier and pleasing to his soul. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/128.\nSpending in the cause of Allah is called a goodly loan. Why?\nمَّن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يُقۡرِضُ ٱللَّهَ قَرۡضًا حَسَنٗا فَيُضَٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥ وَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرٞ كَرِيمٞ ١١\nAl-Qushayri said: A goodly loan is such that the giver spends for charity willingly with sincere intention, seeking Allah's pleasure, not to show off, and spends from honestly-earned money. Al-Qurtubi: 20/244.\nWhat is a goodly loan?\nwords\nمَا يَلِجُWhat penetrates into the earth, like rain\nوَمَا يَعرُجُ فِيهَاWhat ascends to heavens, like angels and deeds\nيُولِجُHe causes to merge\nمِمَّا جَعَلَكُم مُستَخلَفِينَ فِيهِOut of the wealth in which He has made you successive inheritors\nالفَتحِConquest of Makkah\nالحُسنَىParadise\nقَرضًا حَسَنًاA goodly loan, without reminders of generosity or hurtful words"],[539,"§Al-Hadid\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nRecite one page of the Quran with reflection and draw two useful lessons.\nGive to charity with the hope that it will be multiplied on the Day of Resurrection.\nguid\nOn the Day of Resurrection, every servant will be given a light based on his deeds.\nBeware of doubts and suspicions about the religion, for they are signs of hypocrisy.\nStay away from wishful thinking, as it is the asset of those who are bankrupt.\nrefl\nيَوۡمَ تَرَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ يَسۡعَىٰ نُورُهُم بَيۡنَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ\nAbdulla bin Masoud (t) said: \"They will be given light commensurate with their deeds. Some will be given their light as high as a palm tree, for others, it will be as high as a standing person, and the least light given will be as little as the tip of a person’s thumb where it comes on and goes out repeatedly.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/324.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, will the light of the believers vary? On what basis?\nيَوۡمَ يَقُولُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقَٰتُ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱنظُرُونَا نَقۡتَبِسۡ مِن نُّورِكُمۡ قِيلَ ٱرۡجِعُواْ وَرَآءَكُمۡ فَٱلۡتَمِسُواْ نُورٗاۖ\nThis will become the biggest regret and affliction, when one is shown the way to safety and salvation until he believes he is saved and sees the dwellings of those who are destined for bliss, he is cut off from them and overcome with misfortune. We seek refuge with Allah from His wrath and punishment. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/129.\nGiven this verse, explain the mental punishment of hypocrites on the Day of Resurrection.\nيُنَادُونَهُمۡ أَلَمۡ نَكُن مَّعَكُمۡۖ قَالُواْ بَلَىٰ وَلَٰكِنَّكُمۡ فَتَنتُمۡ أَنفُسَكُمۡ وَتَرَبَّصۡتُمۡ وَٱرۡتَبۡتُمۡ وَغَرَّتۡكُمُ ٱلۡأَمَانِيُّ حَتَّىٰ جَآءَ أَمۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَغَرَّكُم بِٱللَّهِ ٱلۡغَرُورُ ١٤\nThe believers will state four basis for the hypocrites' loss, which are: Leading themselves into temptation, awaiting misfortune for the believers, doubting the truthfulness of the Messenger (ﷺ), and deluding themselves with false hopes. Ibn Ashur: 27/385.\nList the four reasons for loss that are stated in this verse.\n۞أَلَمۡ يَأۡنِ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَن تَخۡشَعَ قُلُوبُهُمۡ لِذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ\n(Should be humbled), this means to be in a higher stage of faith, where their hearts soften, calm down, submit, become humiliated and reassured, and turn away from perishable life and seek the eternal one. (At the remembrance of Allah), The Greatest King whose good is the only good, so those who doubt become believers, and those who are weak in faith grow stronger. Hence, the remembrance of Allah (the Quran), becomes remedy for the faith and cure for the sickness of the heart, as Allah's remembrance clears the taints of the hearts. Al-Biqai: 19/279.\nWhat is the best cure for the hardened heart?\nوَلَا يَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِن قَبۡلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡأَمَدُ فَقَسَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡۖ\n(Hardened), due to the passing of time. (Their hearts), became stiffened and bent to the point where they were not prone to obedience and goodness. Al-Qushayri said: Hardness of the heart results from pursuing desires, and clarity of the heart and following desires do not coexist. Al-Biqai: 19/280.\nWhat is the meaning of the hardening of the heart?\nوَلَا يَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِن قَبۡلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡأَمَدُ فَقَسَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡۖ وَكَثِيرٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ فَٰسِقُونَ ١٦\n(Their hearts hardened): Hardening is the beginning of all evil, and it results from one's long heedlessness of Allah. Al-Alusi: 14/181.\nWhat is the risk of the hardening of one's heart?\nٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحۡيِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ مَوۡتِهَاۚ قَدۡ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَعۡقِلُونَ ١٧\nThis description likens the need of the believers' hearts for the remembrance of Allah to the dry land in need of rain, and the effect of the remembrance of Allah in purifying and enlightening the souls to that of the rain reviving the barren land. Ibn Ashur: 27/393.\nWhat is the benefit of being informed that Allah revives the earth after its death?\nwords\nنَقتَبِسWe take\nوَتَرَبَّصتُمand his Companions (ﷺ) You awaited misfortune for the Prophet\nوَغَرَّتكُمُ الأَمَانِيُّYou were deluded by false hopes\nفِديَةٌA ransom from Allah's punishment\nمَأوَاكُمُYour abode\nأَلَم يَأنِHas the time not yet come?"],[540,"§Al-Hadid\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, elevate me to the level of the people of truth.\"\nInvoke Allah to grant you asceticism in this worldly life.\nHasten to be in the first row behind the Imam in all prayers today.\nguid\nKnow that Paradise is a favor from Allah who grants it to whom He wills of His servants.\nBe humble and easy going, for Allah does not like one who is arrogant and conceited.\nKnow that Allah is Free of need and Praiseworthy Who does not need praising from anyone.\nrefl\nٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا لَعِبٞ وَلَهۡوٞ وَزِينَةٞ وَتَفَاخُرُۢ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَتَكَاثُرٞ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰلِ وَٱلۡأَوۡلَٰدِۖ\nThis is confirmed by what you find in the real life of people. In contrast, those who are aware and strive for the Hereafter have hearts that constantly remember Allah, know and love Him; they fill their time with righteous deeds that will bring them closer to Allah. Al-Saadi: 841.\nOnce you know the reality of worldly life, how should you react to that?\nٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا لَعِبٞ وَلَهۡوٞ وَزِينَةٞ وَتَفَاخُرُۢ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَتَكَاثُرٞ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰلِ وَٱلۡأَوۡلَٰدِۖ\nThese are the stages through which every person goes in his life, where play is the stage of childhood, amusement is the stage of juvenile, adornment is the stage of youth, boasting is the stage of middle age, and competition is the stage of old age. Ibn Ashur: 27/401.\nThis verse contains the stages through which people go in their lives. Explain.\nوَفِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ عَذَابٞ شَدِيدٞ وَمَغۡفِرَةٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرِضۡوَٰنٞۚ\nMeaning: In the Hereafter, there can only be one of these two situations: Either a severe punishment in the fire of hell, or forgiveness from Allah for bad deeds, protection from punishment, and the good pleasure of Allah. This is for those who recognized this world for what it was and strove hard for the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 841.\nOnce you know that in the Hereafter there will be either forgiveness or punishment, what should be your position toward this worldly life?\nوَمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡغُرُورِ ٢٠\nSaeed bin Jubair said: This life is an enjoyment of delusion for one who does not seek the reward in the Hereafter, but whoever works in this life for the Hereafter, will enjoy its pleasures until he reaches much better pleasures in the Hereafter. Al-Baghawi: 4/328.\nIs the worldly life an enjoyment of delusion for everyone?\nلِّكَيۡلَا تَأۡسَوۡاْ عَلَىٰ مَا فَاتَكُمۡ وَلَا تَفۡرَحُواْ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخۡتَالٖ فَخُورٍ ٢٣\nMeaning: We made it clear to you that all things are decreed and written before the creation of people, and whatever is written, it will come to pass so that you may not grieve over what you have missed, as missing it is predetermined for you, and one does not miss what he does not long for. You may not exult over what He has given you because when you know that whatever provision and good that is written for you will surely come to pass, your exultation over it will become less. Al-Shanqiti: 7/549.\nKnowing that everything is written before the creation of people provides useful lesson. Explain.\nلِّكَيۡلَا تَأۡسَوۡاْ عَلَىٰ مَا فَاتَكُمۡ وَلَا تَفۡرَحُواْ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخۡتَالٖ فَخُورٍ ٢٣\nIf it is said that a person cannot control himself when it comes to exultation over good things and grieving over what he misses, as when Abu Bakr Al-Siddique (t) was brought abundance of money, he said: \"O Allah, we cannot help but exult over what You made pleasing to us.\" The answer is: The prohibited exultation is that which leads to arrogance and tyranny, and the prohibited grief is that which leads to impatience and resentment. Ibn Juzay: 2/415.\nIn this verse, Allah prohibits exultation over good things and grief over missing them, what is the aim of this prohibition?\nوَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخۡتَالٖ فَخُورٍ ٢٣ ٱلَّذِينَ يَبۡخَلُونَ وَيَأۡمُرُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ بِٱلۡبُخۡلِۗ\nStinginess can be with everything beneficial in religious and worldly things such as wealth , knowledge, etc. One who withholds knowledge from others is stingy with knowledge. The conceited person is the one who is too proud to pursue knowledge, or too proud to teach it to others, which occurs often. The opposite of that is to be humble in pursuing knowledge and generous in teaching it to others. Ibn Taimyah: 6/217.\nMany people are stingy without realizing it. Explain.\nwords\nالصِّدِّيقُونَThe people of the truth\nوَالشُّهَدَاءُMartyrs who are killed in the cause of Allah\nالكُفَّارَSowers, tillers\nيَهِيجُBecomes dry and yellow\nحُطَامًاCrumbled debris\nنَبرَأَهَاWe bring it into existence\nتَأسَواYou grieve"],[541,"§Al-Hadid\ndeeds\nList three manifestations of Allah's might in what you see around you.\nInvoke Allah to help the religion of Islam.\nGive charity for the cause of Islam.\nguid\nThe Heavens and earth were established on justice, so be keen to uphold justice in all of your affairs.\nEvery word and deed in support of Allah's religion is credited for you.\nThe treasures of all bounty and goodness are in the Hands of Allah.\nrefl\nلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا رُسُلَنَا بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَأَنزَلۡنَا مَعَهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَ لِيَقُومَ ٱلنَّاسُ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۖ وَأَنزَلۡنَا ٱلۡحَدِيدَ فِيهِ بَأۡسٞ شَدِيدٞ وَمَنَٰفِعُ لِلنَّاسِ\nThe religion of Islam is based on two things, first: It is what is mentioned by Allah, (and sent down with them the Scripture and the criteria of justice) because this establishes the proofs of the truth, presents the agreement, clarifies ordinances and prohibitions, and rewards and punishments. Second: If the disbelievers persisted in disbelief and denial of Messengers despite clear proofs, then, Allah, the Almighty, sent down the iron, which means that He created it for Sons of Adam so that the believers use it to deter the stubborn disbelievers through killing them by swords, spears, and arrows. Al-Shanqiti: 7/549.\nThe religion of Islam is based on two things. What are they?\nلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا رُسُلَنَا بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَأَنزَلۡنَا مَعَهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡمِيزَانَ لِيَقُومَ ٱلنَّاسُ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۖ وَأَنزَلۡنَا ٱلۡحَدِيدَ فِيهِ بَأۡسٞ شَدِيدٞ وَمَنَٰفِعُ لِلنَّاسِ\nMeaning: We made iron a deterrent for those who refuse the truth and oppose it after the proof has been established against them. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for thirteen years. During that time, the revelation continued being sent to him, containing arguments against the polytheists and explaining the Oneness of Allah with details and proofs. When the evidence was established against those who defied the Messenger(ﷺ), Allah decreed the migration. Then He ordered the believers to fight the disbelievers using swords, using them to strike the necks and foreheads of those who opposed, rejected, and denied the Quran. Ibn Kathir: 4/315.\nThe mention of sending down the Scripture precedes that of iron. Why?\nوَلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَنصُرُهُۥ وَرُسُلَهُۥ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَوِيٌّ عَزِيزٞ ٢٥\nAllah is Self-Sufficient and is in no need of help from anyone, but the believers help Allah's religion. This phrase (and His messengers) is mentioned right after helping Allah's religion to indicate helping the Messengers who convey the Message and their laws and methods. Ibn Ashur: 27/418.\nWhat is meant by helping Allah and His Messengers in this verse?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا فِي قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُ رَأۡفَةٗ وَرَحۡمَةٗۚ\nThe Christians were more gentle and soft-hearted than others when they followed the teachings of Jesus (u). Al-Saadi: 843.\nWhen were the Christians more gentle and soft-hearted toward the believers?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَءَامِنُواْ بِرَسُولِهِۦ يُؤۡتِكُمۡ كِفۡلَيۡنِ مِن رَّحۡمَتِهِ\nMeaning: Fear Allah's punishment because He is the greatest King, put a barrier between yourselves and His wrath by venerating Him, do not feel secure from the plan of Allah, beware of Him taking back what He granted you, follow the Messenger to be saved, and adhere to his teachings, lest you be doomed. Al-Biqai: 19/324.\nWhat is the punishment of those who have no fear of Allah?\nوَيَجۡعَل لَّكُمۡ نُورٗا تَمۡشُونَ بِهِ\nA light means a clear statement and guidance. Ibn Abbas said: It is the Quran. It is, also, said that it is a shining light in which you will walk the Sirat (The bridge across Hell) in the Hereafter. Moreover, it is said that is a light by which you preach Islam to people, thus, becoming leaders in the religion of Islam, and you will not lose your current headship. This was because they feared losing their headship if they followed Muhammad (ﷺ). Al-Qurtubi: 20/278.\nWhat is the light that Allah will make for these people?\nوَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٢٨\nMeaning: Allah is the true and sole owner of this great bounty; no one shares it with Him, nor governs any of it in the least. Hence, Allah selects whom He wills for what He wills, and never anyone can object to that. Al-Biqai: 19/330.\nWhat is the indication of describing Allah as the Possessor of the great bounty?\nwords\nبِالبَيِّنَاتِClear proofs\nوَالمِيزَانَJustice in words and actions\nبَأسٌMight\nعَزِيزٌThe All-Mighty, Victorious\nقَفَّينَا عَلَى آثَارِهِمWe sent following their footsteps\nوَرَهبَانِيَّةًMonasticism\nمَا كَتَبنَاهَاWe did not prescribe it\nفَمَا رَعَوهَاThey did not observe it faithfully\nكِفلَينِDouble portions"],[542,"§Al-Mujadila\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah in humility by saying: \"O Allah, I complain to you of my weakness, lack of support, and the humiliation I am made to receive,\" then, invoke Allah about your worries.\nGive to a charity, help a weak, a destitude or an opressed woman.\nRecall a sin that you committed, then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nAllah's knowledge, His encompassment, and hearing of all sounds are limitless.\nBeware of transgressing the limits of Allah.\nBeware of committing a deed that will distress you on the Day of Resurrection, as every deed is recorded.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعُۢ بَصِيرٌ ١\nThis reveals the perfect nature of Allah's hearing and seeing, and that they encompass all things, small and great. That also indicates that Allah will respond to her complaint and remove her distress. Al-Saadi: 844.\nThe verse concludes with these two holy names. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُظَٰهِرُونَ مِنكُم مِّن نِّسَآئِهِم مَّا هُنَّ أُمَّهَٰتِهِمۡۖ إِنۡ أُمَّهَٰتُهُمۡ إِلَّا ٱلَّٰٓـِٔي وَلَدۡنَهُمۡۚ وَإِنَّهُمۡ لَيَقُولُونَ مُنكَرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ وَزُورٗاۚ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُورٞ ٢\nThese verses make clear that Dhihar [making one's wife unlawful to him by likening her to his mother] is prohibited. In fact, it is said that Dhihar is a major sin because it changes the rule of Allah without His permission, which is even more serious than many major sins. Al-Alusi: 14/200.\nDhihar is described as evil and false. Why?\nوَإِنَّهُمۡ لَيَقُولُونَ مُنكَرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ وَزُورٗاۚ\nDhihar is described as evil and falsehood. The difference between them is that the saying by a husband to his wife, \"You are to me like the back of my mother,\" contains two parts: Informing that she became unlawful to him and initiating an evil statement. Falsehood is untruth, which is the opposite of the firmed truth, and evil is the opposite of good. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/139.\nDhihar is described as evil and false. Why?\nذَٰلِكَ لِتُؤۡمِنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِه\nThis ruling that We have explained and clarified to you is so that you may truly believe in Allah and His Messenger by adhering to this and other rulings, and acting in accordance with them. Adherence to the rulings of Allah and acting in accordance with them is part of faith; indeed, it is the aim of faith and is one of the things that cause faith to increase, develop and become complete. Al-Saadi: 844.\nGiven this verse, explain the link between righteous deeds and faith.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَآدُّونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ كُبِتُواْ كَمَا كُبِتَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۚ\nMeaning: They are doomed. Qatadah said: They have been disgraced like the ones before them have. It is said that they have been punished. Moreover, it is said that they have been enraged in the Battle of the Trench. It is also said that they will be debased, which is a glad tidings of victory from Allah to the believers. Al-Qurtubi: 20/305.\nWhat is meant by (abased)? What is the glad tidings in this verse?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحَآدُّونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ كُبِتُواْ كَمَا كُبِتَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۚ وَقَدۡ أَنزَلۡنَآ ءَايَٰتِۢ بَيِّنَٰتٖۚ وَلِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٥\nIt is evident that those who oppose Allah and His Messenger are abased, disgraced, full of rage and sorrow, and doomed. This occurs only when they hide their opposition for fear of being killed; otherwise, those who, openly, show their opposition and feel secure about their lives and wealth, are not abased, rather, they are happy and joyous. Allah says, (are abased as those before them were abased), the ones before them were those who opposed the Messengers and Allah's Messenger were abased by a punishment from Allah, or at the hands of the believers. Ibn Taimyah: 6/240.\nOpposing Allah and His Messenger results in sicknesses of the heart in this life and Allah's punishment in the Hereafter. Explain.\nيَوۡمَ يَبۡعَثُهُمُ ٱللَّهُ جَمِيعٗا فَيُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا عَمِلُوٓاْۚ أَحۡصَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُ وَنَسُوهُۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ شَهِيدٌ ٦\nThe statement (Allah has kept their complete record, while they have forgotten it) serves as an answer to a hidden question that says: How Will Allah inform them of their deeds that are so abundant and diverse? The answer is: Allah had enumerated all of it and nothing is missed by Him. They forgot it and did not keep track of it, but they will find it present before them in their Records. Al-Shawkani: 5/186.\nThe statement (Allah has kept their complete record, while they have forgotten it) is an answer to a hidden question. What is it?\nwords\nتُجَادِلُكَShe argues with you, Khawla bint Tha'labah\nزَوجِهَاHer Husband, Aws bin Al-Samit\nوَزُورًاFalsehood\nفَتَحرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍFreeing of a believing slave, a male or female\nيَتَمَآسَّاTouch each other in intimacy\nيُحَآدُّونَThose who Oppose\nكُبِتُواAre abased and humiliated"]])